    "https://muw.peopleadmin.com/postings/7054": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Chemistry",
      "description": "Mississippi University for Women | Assistant or Associate Professor of Chemistry Skip to Main Content Home About The W ACADEMICS & MAJORS Admissions SUPPORT NEWS Directories . Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Employment Non-Faculty Employment Student Employment Assistant or Associate Professor of Chemistry Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Being authorized to work in the United States is a precondition of employment, and MUW does not sponsor work visas. To be eligible for this position, you will need to be authorized to work in the U.S. on a full-time basis now and in the future. MUW does not hire individuals who require employer sponsored visas. Consideration of complete applications will begin Nov 1, 2026, and continue until a successful candidate is hired. For more information about the position, contact Dr. Xiaoxia Li (662) 329-8561 or email xli@muw.edu. Visit the link https://muw.peopleadmin.com to upload required documents for application. Please provide: CV Cover letter Statement of teaching philosophy (no more than 2 pages) Plan for undergraduate-centered research in Organic Chemistry (no more than 2 pages) Information for three contacts that can provide reference letters Documents should be uploaded in the \"Applicant Documents Section” under “Other Documents”. Position Justification Position Information Position Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Chemistry Unit Name Sciences and Mathematics Salary Grade Faculty Number of Months 9 months Full-time or Part-time Full-Time Hours per week 40 Annual Salary or Hourly Rate Range Essential Duties The successful candidate will teach Organic Chemistry , General Chemistry, instrumental courses and courses in their area of expertise. Service to the department, university, and community is expected along with a commitment to the scholarship of teaching and learning at a diverse, primarily undergraduate institution. Applications should also have a viable research plan that incorporates undergraduate involvement. Additional start-up funding from NIH’s MS- INBRE (IDeA Network of Biomedical Research Excellence) might be available if the research area relates to biomedical or public health fields. Applicants may be considered that are near the completion of their doctoral degree, but completion of their degree within a year (August 2028) will be required for their continued employment. In addition to campus resources, Interactions and collaborations are also possible with Mississippi State University, a Research-I institution that is a 25-minute drive from campus. Minimum Qualifications It is preferred that applicants have a doctorate in organic chemistry, or a related chemistry field, and a commitment to the scholarship of teaching and learning. Job Description Summary Applications are invited for a tenure-track position in ORGANIC CHEMISTRY at either Assistant Professor or Associate Professor level, commensurate with experience, beginning August 2027. To enter at the Associate Professor level, candidates must have several years of undergraduate teaching experience and a track record of involving undergraduates in research projects. The successful candidate will teach Organic Chemistry , General Chemistry, instrumental courses, and courses in their area of expertise. Service to the department, university, and community is expected along with a commitment to the scholarship of teaching and learning at a diverse, primarily undergraduate institution. Applications should also have a viable research plan that incorporates undergraduate involvement. Additional start-up funding from NIH’s MS- INBRE (IDeA Network of Biomedical Research Excellence) might be available if the research area relates to biomedical or public health fields. Applicants may be considered that are near the completion of their doctoral degree, but completion of their degree within a year (August 2028) will be required for their continued employment. In addition to campus resources, Interactions and collaborations are also possible with Mississippi State University, a Research-I institution that is a 25-minute drive from campus. Mississippi University for Women ( MUW ) is a public coeducational, primarily undergraduate, liberal arts institution serving an economically and racially diverse student body with a total annual enrollment of over 2200 students. The University emphasizes a student-centered learning environment that includes research opportunities. Additional information can be found on the MUW website: http://www.muw.edu . All hires contingent upon successful completion of a background check. Mississippi University for Women is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Background Check Statement Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. However, failure to disclose may disqualify a candidate. Requisition Detail Information Requisition Number FY20285F Open Date 09/10/2026 Will this job have a specific close date? No Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Being authorized to work in the United States is a precondition of employment, and MUW does not sponsor work visas. To be eligible for this position, you will need to be authorized to work in the U.S. on a full-time basis now and in the future. MUW does not hire individuals who require employer sponsored visas. Consideration of complete applications will begin Nov 1, 2026, and continue until a successful candidate is hired. For more information about the position, contact Dr. Xiaoxia Li (662) 329-8561 or email xli@muw.edu. Visit the link https://muw.peopleadmin.com to upload required documents for application. Please provide: CV Cover letter Statement of teaching philosophy (no more than 2 pages) Plan for undergraduate-centered research in Organic Chemistry (no more than 2 pages) Information for three contacts that can provide reference letters Documents should be uploaded in the \"Applicant Documents Section” under “Other Documents”. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? MUW Departmental Announcement MUW Human Resources Office MUW Website Mississippi Employment Service Local Newspaper In-state Newspaper Out-of-state Newspaper The Chronicle of Higher Education HigherEdJobs.com Friend Journal/Periodical Off-campus Recruitment Women/Minority Publication Contacted by department and invited to apply Other The Academic Network (TAN) * Are you currently authorized to work in the United States? (Proof of Citizenship or Immigration status will be required upon offer of employment) Yes No * If hired, would you need sponsorship or work authorization to work for MUW now or in the future? (NOTE: MUW does not sponsor employment visas.) Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Transcript 1 Other Document Optional Documents Unofficial Transcript 2 Unofficial Transcript 3 © 2013 Mississippi University for Women Columbus, MS 39701 / 662-329-7106 Non Discriminating Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
